---
layout: layouts/feature.njk
wide: true
playgroundCta: true
newsletterSignup: true
hideBreadcrumbs: true
title: Features | Shellui
description: "Build web apps with shared navigation, sign-in, administration, and file storage. Explore Shellui, an open-source microfrontend shell."
heading: "Build your app. Share the essentials."
lede: "Shellui is an open-source shell that brings your web apps together with shared navigation, sign-in, administration, email, and file storage. Your apps run inside embedded pages called iframes, using the frameworks you choose."
---

<div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-pretty text-foreground sm:text-3xl">A shared foundation for your web apps</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Build a customer portal, an internal tool, or a product with several apps. Configure the navigation, layout, and connected services in <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">shellui.config.json</code>. Each app keeps its own interface and uses the Shellui software development kit (SDK) to access shared features.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Start with navigation and a layout, then connect authentication or storage when your project needs them. Shellui is MIT-licensed and free to run. You can host the shell and its services on your own infrastructure.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Explore the features below, or try the <a class="font-medium text-primary-ink underline underline-offset-2" href="{{ site.playground }}">playground</a> in your browser before installing anything.</p>
    <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
      <a href="/architecture/" class="font-medium text-primary-ink underline underline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary">Architecture</a>
      ·
      <a href="{{ site.docs }}" class="font-medium text-primary-ink underline underline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary">Docs</a>
      ·
      <a href="{{ site.playground }}" class="font-medium text-primary-ink underline underline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Playground</a>
      ·
      <a href="/changelog/" class="font-medium text-primary-ink underline underline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary">Changelog</a>
    </p>
  </div>

<div class="mt-16 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-6">
  {% for item in featurePages %}
    <a
      id="{{ item.id }}"
      href="{{ item.href }}"
      class="group anim-card flex min-w-0 flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-border bg-card focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary{% if loop.index == 1 %} sm:col-span-2 lg:col-span-4{% elif loop.index == 2 %} lg:col-span-2{% elif loop.last %} sm:col-span-2 lg:col-span-3{% else %} lg:col-span-3{% endif %}"
    >
      {% set bleed = item.visual in ["apps-visual", "upload"] %}
      <div class="border-b border-border bg-muted{% if bleed %} overflow-hidden{% if item.visual != "apps-visual" %} aspect-[3/2] [&_svg]:h-full{% endif %}{% else %} p-4 sm:p-5{% endif %}">
        <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[16rem] {% if item.visual == 'auth' %}max-w-[13rem]{% endif %}{% if item.visual == 'toaster' or bleed %}max-w-none{% endif %}{% if bleed %} h-full{% endif %}">
          {% if item.visual == "toaster" %}
            {% include "feature-visual-toaster.njk" %}
          {% elif item.visual == "shell-layout" %}
            {% include "shell-layout-anim.njk" %}
          {% elif item.visual == "auth" %}
            {% include "feature-visual-auth.njk" %}
          {% elif item.visual == "admin" %}
            {% include "feature-visual-admin.njk" %}
          {% elif item.visual == "apps-visual" %}
            {% set avBare = true %}<div class="av4-hov hidden lg:block">{% include "apps-visual-v4.njk" %}</div><div class="lg:hidden">{% include "apps-visual-v4-thumb.njk" %}</div>
          {% elif item.visual == "upload" %}
            {% set upSlice = true %}{% include "feature-visual-upload.njk" %}
          {% elif item.visual == "storage" %}
            {% include "feature-visual-storage.njk" %}
          {% elif item.visual == "email" %}
            {% include "feature-visual-email.njk" %}
          {% elif item.visual == "ship" %}
            {% include "feature-visual-ship.njk" %}
          {% endif %}
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-1 flex-col p-6">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-pretty text-foreground">{{ item.title }}</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">{{ item.benefit }}</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          {% for point in item.points %}
            <li>{{ point }}</li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
        <span class="mt-6 inline-flex items-center text-sm font-medium text-primary-ink group-hover:underline">{{ item.cta }}</span>
      </div>
    </a>
  {% endfor %}
</div>

<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="webhooks">
  <div class="grid items-start gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1.1fr)_minmax(0,0.9fr)] lg:gap-16">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <h2 id="webhooks" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-pretty text-foreground sm:text-3xl">One webhook system</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">identity-service, storage-service, hosting-service, and email-service send signed webhooks. You write the rules in Administration, and you can point a rule at an n8n workflow. You see the signing secret once. The service image retries failed deliveries every minute, so you do not add cron.</p>
      <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        <a href="/features/administration/#webhooks" class="font-medium text-primary-ink underline underline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary">Webhooks in Administration</a>
        ·
        <a href="{{ site.docs }}/identity/n8n" class="font-medium text-primary-ink underline underline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary">n8n guide</a>
        ·
        <a href="/features/email/#rules" class="font-medium text-primary-ink underline underline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary">Email rules</a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-foreground">The same on every service:</p>
      <ul class="mt-4 max-w-md space-y-4 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">
        <li><span class="font-medium text-foreground">Standard Webhooks</span>: each delivery includes <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">webhook-id</code>, <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">webhook-timestamp</code>, and <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">webhook-signature</code>.</li>
        <li><span class="font-medium text-foreground">Retries</span>: the image retries failed deliveries every minute, up to 8 attempts.</li>
        <li><span class="font-medium text-foreground">n8n</span>: use a Webhook node as the receiver, and send a test event from Administration.</li>
        <li><span class="font-medium text-foreground">Sign-in links</span>: webhook bodies do not include a magic link or its token.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
